{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/963682-questions-about-the-wyrm","id":963682,"title":"questions about The Wyrm","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-09-05T07:22:01-07:00","id":963682,"title":"questions about The Wyrm","content":"Is he awake, is he sleeping or both?<br /> how does it lives? what about the heads of the wyrm?<br /> how does fomorol works, i mean, how do you put a bane inside a chemical?<br /> is there any physical descriptions of how The Wyrm looks like? or any ilustrations?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-05T09:30:09-07:00","id":963737,"title":"","content":"The Wyrm of Corruption could be considered to be the 'local' manifestation of a Cosmic principle of Destruction or Entropy. Presumably the Wyrm of Balance exists outside of the Sol System but has quarantined itself from the cancer that is the Wyrm of Corruption, it largely depends on how universal you want to make Fera mythology and which version of Fera mythology you want to go with. It 'feeds' off of destruction and entropy, though it also feeds off of Corruption.<br /> <br /> The Wyrm of Corruption is a fragmented entity, with each 'head' being a distinct entity that is still part of the Wyrm of Corruption. Some of the parts are imprisoned, some of the parts are sleeping, some of the parts are active in the Umbra. None of them are active in the Material World because that would be a Global Extinction Event. It is an entity of nearly infinite power, and that is if it only a quarantined part of a greater Wyrm of Balance, so it is difficult to describe except that it makes Cthulu look like a sweet little puppy dog by comparison.<br /> <br /> The creation of bane materials is actually quite simple. Every material object has a quiescent spirit within it, sleeping until it is Awakened, usually be a supernatural creature. If you Awaken the spirit of a material object and then store that object in an area of extreme corruption, the spirit will become a Bane over time. Then you shatter the Bane by grind the material object into dust and contaminating consumer goods with the dust. Anyone who ingests the contaminated object has a small chance of having the Bane reform within their body and, when it does, it will attempt to take over its host before it is expelled. The bodies of fomori can also be used to contaminate objects to weaken resistance against Bane possession.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-05T09:39:39-07:00","id":963742,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/963682-questions-about-the-wyrm#post963682\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Is he awake, is he sleeping or both?<br /> how does it lives?</div> </div> </div> </div>Neither awake nor asleep, and it doesn't really &quot;live&quot;. The Wyrm is a Cosmic entity/force.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/963682-questions-about-the-wyrm#post963682\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> what about the heads of the wyrm?</div> </div> </div> </div>The heads of the Wyrm are individual entities (Beast of War, Eater of Souls, Defiler) and they do &quot;live&quot; sort of. Book of the Wyrm 20 goes into decent detail on them.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/963682-questions-about-the-wyrm#post963682\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> how does fomorol works, i mean, how do you put a bane inside a chemical?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, supposedly it's made from recycled fomori, not banes specifically. It works though, because it is a Wyrm enhancer produced in Malfeas.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/963682-questions-about-the-wyrm#post963682\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> is there any physical descriptions of how The Wyrm looks like? or any ilustrations?</div> </div> </div> </div> There are a few different illustrations. Since the Wyrm is an abstraction, and visual representations are subject to the artist's interpretation (in and out of character). My favorite illustration is in the Art of Werewolf. Its the piece by Ron Spencer on the left page under &quot;The Triat&quot;. I'm not sure which book it was first in, and I couldn't find the picture online to link, but it's in the Art book.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-05T10:04:45-07:00","id":963758,"title":"","content":"The Wyrm: This is kind of a rough question... The Wyrm is a spirit entity that represents one of the three tenets of existence: entropy/destruction (The Wyld being creation/change and the Weaver being stability/stasis/existence). It's probably best not to think of any of the Triat (Wyrm, Wyld and Weaver) as a big monster sitting on a throne somewhere. They might have a core being of some sort, but are certainly able to divide their attention and presence in addition to having an almost limitless supply of subservient spirits representing them that they gradually spawn. Similarly, their minds certainly don't work like a human's.. they are sentient forces, making them far more and yet far less complicated than a person. The Wyrm as a whole is trapped and mad, likely to a point beyond consciousness or rational thought... but each of the heads is awake, active, and plotting.<br /> <br /> The Heads of the Wyrm: Now, that said, the Wyrm is arguably more manageable as an opponent because of its madness and its 'heads'. The Weaver went crazy and trapped the Wyrm in a web, and the Wyrm is constantly trying to escape by pushing itself through the gaps in the web... the result being numerous lesser entities mentally disconnected from one another (often to the point of direct conflict) but each trying to live out some aspect of the original. These are EACH still apocalyptic, world-destroying powers that are certainly up there with the planetary incaerna (the spirit of a planet) on the power-scale. Defeating or destroying any single hydra head, urge wyrm, or any other aspect of the Wyrm would be the central storyline for a long-term game of massive and epic proportions that is far more likely to end in death and defeat than victory.<br /> <br /> A Giant Wall of Text Introduction to Fomorol: Based on your signature, you're familiar with Wraith, so use that as a starting point when thinking of the Wyrm, spirits and banes. (I'm about to grossly oversimplify for brevity) Spirits are just spiritual representations of ideas (ideas of emotions, objects, beliefs, animals, substances, etc). Banes are spirits, but those attached to a Wyrm-aspected idea: decay, destruction, corruption, suffering, hate, lust... sin and entropy, in general. Wraiths are also spirits in WtA cosmology, just ones attached to the idea of a person (and their death). Since the penumbra overlaps with the physical world, think of it as yet another layer like the Shadowlands... maybe if the Shadowlands are a step to the left of physical reality, the penumbra is a step to the right. Spirits can colocate and inhabit physical items, making talens (one-shot magic items) and fetishes (permanent magic items) and thereby imbuing them with an ability similar to the spirit's nature (a stone elemental making armor extra tough; a spirit of rage letting a weapon's weilder enter a berserk frenzy, a spear that shoots lightning, a flute that calms listeners, etc). The spirit of an existing object can also be Awakened so that its own natural attributes become enhanced, like a talen but where the item and the spirit already match (alcohol that gets you super drunk, medicinal herbs that cause supernatural healing, etc). Spirits can on rare occasion enter objects willingly, or more commonly some type of mystical ritual binds or awakens the spirit. Fomorol is a substance made from a similar process, resulting in a spirit-imbued chemical that's empowered by a bane (or by the bane energy in the corpses of their dead hosts).<br /> <br /> Appearance of the Wyrm: I don't think there are any definite physical descriptions of the Wyrm itself, apart from the fact that it's trapped in the Weaver's web and has split its head into a Hydra trying to get out. Again, keep in mind this is a spiritual entity representing a third of the fundamental laws of the universe, existing on a scale much like Oblivion itself. Its physical embodiment likely exists in a distant spirit realm, planetary in scale, with altered laws of physics and warped reality, surrounded by a legion of spirit followers, and possessing beyond-godlike powers... both active and inadvertent. Meeting it would probably twist, madden or destroy any being to lay eyes on it. Somehow killing it MIGHT end the universe as we know it... either immediately or eventually... as defining laws of reality change or disappear.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my mediocre WoD/Aeon/Exalted art at <a href=\"http://blackspinel.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://blackspinel.deviantart.com</a> ! It'll make you go &quot;Yup! That's pretty mediocre!&quot;","edited":{"userid":12162,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12162-crusher-of-cities","user":"Crusher-of-Cities","date":".  Typos... typos everywhere. 09-05-2016, 01:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12162-crusher-of-cities","name":"Crusher-of-Cities","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12162_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-05T18:30:33-07:00","id":964002,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/963682-questions-about-the-wyrm?p=963737#post963737\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Wyrm of Corruption could be considered to be the 'local' manifestation of a Cosmic principle of Destruction or Entropy. Presumably the Wyrm of Balance exists outside of the Sol System but has quarantined itself from the cancer that is the Wyrm of Corruption, it largely depends on how universal you want to make Fera mythology and which version of Fera mythology you want to go with. It 'feeds' off of destruction and entropy, though it also feeds off of Corruption.</div> </div> </div> </div>It does not presumably dwell somewhere out in space. It's where the rest of the Wyrm is: in Malfeas, trapped and unable to do anything about its predicament. You get there by going into the Deep Umbra. The Werewolf Deep Umbra, which isn't outer space, not the Mage Deep Umbra that is. The latter is covered in Werewolf by the Aetherial Realm, which is the extraterrestrial Penumbra.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Wyrm of Corruption is a fragmented entity, with each 'head' being a distinct entity that is still part of the Wyrm of Corruption. Some of the parts are imprisoned, some of the parts are sleeping, some of the parts are active in the Umbra. None of them are active in the Material World because that would be a Global Extinction Event. It is an entity of nearly infinite power, and that is if it only a quarantined part of a greater Wyrm of Balance, so it is difficult to describe except that it makes Cthulu look like a sweet little puppy dog by comparison. </div> </div> </div>Maeljin Incarnae under the Urge Wyrms sometimes do manifest. The Croatan also prevented a manifestation of the Eater of Souls from occurring. None of the parts are really sleeping, though; all of them are ardently listening and searching for whatever angle they can use to get ahead in the twisted hierarchy that's sprung up around the fragmentation of the greater being. Even the sacrifice of the Croatan doesn't make the EoS inactive in any real way. It &quot;just&quot; separates it from the physical world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T08:36:05-07:00","id":964978,"title":"","content":"I think describing the Wyrm's &quot;core&quot; would be <i>extremely</i> difficult, given how both transcendent <i>and</i> mangled it is thanks to the Weaver. However, as that's not a very fun answer:<br /> <br /> Imagine <i>beneath</i> Malfeas a vast, continent-sized Shape lay, perfectly still, encrusted with so much Weaver-made webs as to make the Gauntlet seem nonexistent. It is CRUSHINGLY tight, these webs; they're stained green with the Wyrm's radioactive blood. No sound emerges from within, and the shape is vaguely serpentine.<br /> <br /> There is, however, a single, nigh-microscopic <i>gap</i> in the webbing, from which blasts an apocalyptic vent of balefire and Essence so corrupt as to poison a Yama King (who are, <i>themselves</i>!, highly corrupt)! From this gash issues forth...Malfeas. The entirety of Malfeas stands revealed as the viscera of the Wyrm, it's blood and guts slowly emptying out into the Umbra!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T18:36:45-07:00","id":965401,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demigod Beast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/963682-questions-about-the-wyrm?p=964978#post964978\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think describing the Wyrm's &quot;core&quot; would be <i>extremely</i> difficult, given how both transcendent <i>and</i> mangled it is thanks to the Weaver. However, as that's not a very fun answer:<br /> <br /> Imagine <i>beneath</i> Malfeas a vast, continent-sized Shape lay, perfectly still, encrusted with so much Weaver-made webs as to make the Gauntlet seem nonexistent. It is CRUSHINGLY tight, these webs; they're stained green with the Wyrm's radioactive blood. No sound emerges from within, and the shape is vaguely serpentine.<br /> <br /> There is, however, a single, nigh-microscopic <i>gap</i> in the webbing, from which blasts an apocalyptic vent of balefire and Essence so corrupt as to poison a Yama King (who are, <i>themselves</i>!, highly corrupt)! From this gash issues forth...Malfeas. The entirety of Malfeas stands revealed as the viscera of the Wyrm, it's blood and guts slowly emptying out into the Umbra!</div> </div> </div> </div>Reading, I heard it in <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=rHaUrSJdjIc\" target=\"_blank\">Wayne June's voice.</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}